### Summary

This is a small, well-scoped diff (commit `8fa7491`, "feat(deepen): wire the deepen skill into review and implementation, mirroring distill"): the frozen scope's only code change is one line in `engine/src/core/model-profiles.ts` (adding `"deepen"` as the required skill for `architecture-tech-lead` in `AGENT_CATALOG`), a doc-comment update in `helpers.ts`, and an existing test's fixture prompt updated to keep passing. The remaining files are prompt/doc content (README, agents/architecture-tech-lead.md, commands/review-pr.md, skills/*.md) with no directly-applicable unit tests.

The single behavioral change is covered almost entirely for free by pre-existing drift-proof infrastructure:
- `engine/tests/core/required-skill-policy.test.ts` iterates `AGENT_REQUIRED_SKILLS` data-driven (`it.each`), so the new `architecture-tech-lead → "deepen"` entry automatically gets three checks: the skill exists on disk, `agents/architecture-tech-lead.md` frontmatter declares it, and `requiredSkillMarker("deepen")` satisfies the real `checkAgentSkillPrompt` gate for both the marked (pass) and unmarked (fail) cases.
- `engine/tests/core/agent-catalog.test.ts` proves `AGENT_REQUIRED_SKILLS` stays a faithful projection of `AGENT_POLICIES`.
- `engine/tests/pi-extension-review-events.test.ts`'s updated graphless-spawn test exercises the real `pi/extension.ts` module end-to-end with `architecture-tech-lead`, so the wiring is proven through the actual spawn path, not just unit-level.

I checked for stale fixtures elsewhere in the suite that hardcode `architecture-tech-lead`'s prior `requiredSkill: null` (which would now be silently wrong) — found none; every `requiredSkill: null` fixture I traced belongs to a different, unaffected role (`code-reviewer`, `type-design-analyzer`, `review-verifier-agent`, etc.).

